<?php

$baseDetails = [
    'A useful project plan should connect the visible experience to the operational reality behind it. The page, form, dashboard, or workflow is only the part people see. Behind it are approvals, notifications, data rules, reporting habits, and maintenance decisions that decide whether the project stays useful.',
    'For non-technical teams, the best preparation is plain language. Describe what happens now, what should happen instead, who is responsible, and what information must be trusted. A developer can turn that into screens, database tables, jobs, permissions, and integrations.',
    'The first version should reduce uncertainty. If the business does not yet know which workflow matters most, build a smaller version that creates feedback quickly. If the workflow is already proven, invest more in reliability, permissions, and reporting.',
    'A good build also needs an owner after launch. Someone should know how to update content, review leads, check reports, respond to errors, and decide what improves next. Without ownership, even a well-built system slowly becomes harder to trust.',
];

$makeSections = function (array $headings, string $topic): array {
    return collect($headings)->map(function (string $heading) use ($topic): array {
        return [
            'heading' => $heading,
            'body' => "{$heading} matters when planning {$topic} because it changes the work that happens after the first version goes live. It affects what the user sees, what the business controls, and what the developer must protect in the background.",
            'points' => [
                "Define how {$heading} affects the first useful version.",
                'Write the current manual process before choosing software features.',
                'Separate must-have decisions from improvements that can wait.',
                'Decide how the result will be measured after launch.',
                'Keep the owner, staff, customer, and developer responsibilities clear.',
            ],
        ];
    })->all();
};

$post = function (
    int $day,
    int $slot,
    string $title,
    string $slug,
    string $category,
    array $tags,
    string $intent,
    string $audience,
    string $opening,
    string $context,
    array $headings,
    string $example,
    string $cta,
    string $imageSlug,
) use ($baseDetails, $makeSections): array {
    return [
        'day' => $day,
        'slot' => $slot,
        'title' => $title,
        'slug' => $slug,
        'category' => $category,
        'tags' => $tags,
        'search_intent' => $intent,
        'meta_title' => str($title)->limit(58, '')->rtrim(' ,:-')->toString(),
        'meta_description' => str("Practical guide for {$audience} on {$intent}, with examples, planning advice, mistakes, checklist, and soft next steps.")->limit(156, '')->rtrim(' ,:-')->append('.')->toString(),
        'excerpt' => str("A practical, business-focused guide to {$intent}, written for {$audience} who want clear decisions before spending money on web development.")->limit(230)->toString(),
        'keywords' => [$intent, $category, 'web development consulting', 'Youssef Youyou'],
        'audience' => $audience,
        'opening' => $opening,
        'context' => $context,
        'sections' => $makeSections($headings, $intent),
        'details' => $baseDetails,
        'example' => $example,
        'mistakes' => [
            'Starting with tools before the business workflow is clear.',
            'Treating every idea as a version-one requirement.',
            'Ignoring who will update, review, and maintain the project after launch.',
            'Skipping analytics, form testing, permissions, or launch checks because they feel small.',
            'Choosing the cheapest path without understanding what risk is being accepted.',
        ],
        'checklist' => [
            'Write the business goal in one sentence.',
            'Name the primary user and the first action they need to complete.',
            'List the required content, data, access, and integrations.',
            'Separate must-have features from later improvements.',
            'Decide how success will be reviewed after launch.',
            'Prepare a soft CTA or next step that matches the project goal.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['How technical does the plan need to be?', 'It does not need to be written like a developer specification. A clear business workflow, user journey, feature priority list, and examples are enough to start a useful technical conversation.'],
            ['Can this start small?', 'Yes. Most serious web projects should start with the smallest professional version that can be used, measured, and improved without rebuilding the foundation.'],
            ['When should I contact a developer?', 'Contact a developer when the business goal is clear enough to discuss tradeoffs, or when you need help turning a vague idea into a realistic scope before spending heavily.'],
        ],
        'cta' => $cta,
        'image_slug' => $imageSlug,
    ];
};

return [
    $post(1, 0, 'What to Include in a Business Website Brief Before Hiring a Developer', 'business-website-brief-before-hiring-developer', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'Client Acquisition', 'SEO'], 'what to prepare before hiring web developer', 'business owners and founders preparing to hire a developer', 'A good website brief does not need to be long, but it needs to be honest. It should explain what the business does, who the site is for, what action matters, and which constraints the developer should know before estimating.', 'Many website projects begin with vague requests such as “I need a modern site” or “I want something like this competitor.” A better brief turns that first conversation into a practical planning session.', ['Define the business goal', 'Describe the target visitor', 'List required pages and content', 'Explain functionality and integrations', 'Share references without copying them', 'Prepare budget and timeline context', 'Questions to ask before approving a proposal'], 'A consulting company might think it needs a five-page site. The brief reveals that the real need is better service positioning, lead qualification, case-style project pages, analytics, and a contact form that asks about budget and timeline.', 'If you are preparing a business website brief and want a developer who can turn it into a practical build plan, contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'what-to-prepare-before-hiring-web-developer'),
    $post(1, 1, 'How to Know If Your Business Needs a Website, Dashboard, or Full Web App', 'business-needs-website-dashboard-or-web-app', 'Business Automation', ['Business Automation', 'Dashboard', 'Custom Software'], 'website vs dashboard vs web app', 'non-technical business owners choosing the right type of project', 'Not every digital project should become a full application. Some businesses need a clearer website. Some need an internal dashboard. Some need a custom web app because users, data, and workflows are part of the product.', 'Choosing the wrong type of project creates waste. A simple site can become overloaded with custom logic, while a real business application can be underplanned as if it were only a set of pages.', ['Simple website use cases', 'When a dashboard is enough', 'When a full web app is required', 'Cost and maintenance differences', 'Data and user account considerations', 'How to decide before requesting a quote'], 'A logistics business may need a website for trust, a dashboard for internal delivery status, and later a customer portal. Building all three at once may be too much, but naming the layers helps plan the roadmap.', 'Need help choosing between a website, dashboard, portal, or full Laravel web app? I can help you scope the right first version at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'laravel-dashboard-understand-business'),
    $post(1, 2, 'The Founder’s Guide to Planning a SaaS MVP in 30 Days', 'founders-guide-planning-saas-mvp-30-days', 'SaaS & MVP', ['SaaS', 'MVP', 'Startup'], 'plan SaaS MVP', 'SaaS founders who need a practical planning roadmap', 'A 30-day SaaS MVP plan should not be a rushed build. It should be a focused period for narrowing the user, defining the paid workflow, choosing the first version, and preparing the feedback loop.', 'Founders often lose time because the idea keeps expanding. A short planning window forces decisions: what the product does first, what stays manual, and what must be measured after launch.', ['Week one: user and problem clarity', 'Week two: workflow and feature priority', 'Week three: prototype and technical plan', 'Week four: launch preparation', 'What not to build in the MVP', 'Feedback plan after launch'], 'A founder building proposal software may start with templates, e-signatures, AI, payments, analytics, and teams. A 30-day plan can reduce version one to creating, sending, and tracking proposals for one type of customer.', 'If you are planning a SaaS MVP and want help turning it into a focused Laravel product roadmap, contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'build-saas-mvp-without-wasting-budget'),
    $post(2, 0, 'Why Most Business Websites Do Not Convert Visitors Into Leads', 'why-business-websites-do-not-convert-leads', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'Client Acquisition', 'SEO'], 'why website does not convert', 'business owners with traffic but weak inquiries', 'A website can have traffic and still fail as a sales asset. Visitors leave when they do not understand the offer, do not trust the business, cannot find proof, or feel friction before contacting.', 'Conversion problems are rarely caused by one button color. They usually come from unclear positioning, weak pages, poor mobile experience, slow loading, missing proof, and forms that do not match buyer intent.', ['Unclear offer and weak positioning', 'Poor calls to action', 'Missing trust signals', 'Slow mobile experience', 'Forms that ask the wrong questions', 'Analytics gaps that hide the real issue'], 'A marketing agency might get visitors from search but few leads because the service pages use vague language. Rewriting pages around buyer questions and adding proof near the form can matter more than adding another animation.', 'If your business website gets visitors but not enough qualified inquiries, I can help diagnose and rebuild the conversion path. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'business-website-before-running-ads'),
    $post(2, 1, 'How a Custom CRM Helps Service Businesses Follow Up Better', 'custom-crm-service-business-follow-up', 'Business Automation', ['CRM', 'Business Automation', 'Dashboard'], 'custom CRM for service business', 'service business owners managing leads and follow-ups', 'Follow-up is where many service businesses lose revenue quietly. Leads arrive from forms, referrals, calls, social media, or WhatsApp, but the next action is not always tracked.', 'A custom CRM can turn scattered communication into a clear pipeline: new lead, qualified lead, quote sent, follow-up due, won, lost, or postponed.', ['Lead capture and source tracking', 'Follow-up reminders', 'Customer history', 'Quote and invoice connection', 'Team task ownership', 'Pipeline reporting for the owner'], 'A repair company may receive twenty inquiries a week but only follow up with the easiest ones. A CRM can show who is waiting, who needs a quote, and which sources produce better clients.', 'If your service business needs a CRM that matches the way your team follows up, I can build it around your real workflow. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'custom-crm-small-business'),
    $post(2, 2, 'Laravel for SaaS MVPs: When It Makes Sense and When It Does Not', 'laravel-for-saas-mvps-when-it-makes-sense', 'Laravel', ['Laravel', 'SaaS', 'MVP'], 'Laravel for SaaS MVP', 'founders comparing technology choices for a SaaS MVP', 'Laravel can be an excellent choice for a SaaS MVP, especially when the product needs accounts, billing-ready structure, dashboards, notifications, jobs, APIs, and relational data. It is not always the right answer for every product.', 'The right stack should lower project risk. For many business SaaS products, Laravel gives useful structure without forcing unnecessary complexity.', ['Where Laravel is strong for SaaS', 'When Laravel may be too much', 'Authentication, billing, and teams', 'Queues, email, and background work', 'Admin dashboards and reporting', 'Long-term maintenance considerations'], 'A B2B subscription tool with accounts, reports, invoices, and admin workflows is a strong Laravel fit. A heavy real-time collaboration product may need different architecture choices early.', 'If you are deciding whether Laravel fits your SaaS MVP, I can help you evaluate the workflow, budget, and first build. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'laravel-business-applications-strong-choice'),
    $post(3, 0, 'How to Plan an Admin Dashboard That Your Team Will Actually Use', 'plan-admin-dashboard-team-will-use', 'Business Automation', ['Dashboard', 'Business Automation', 'Productivity'], 'admin dashboard planning', 'business owners and managers planning internal dashboards', 'An admin dashboard is useful only if the team uses it during real work. If it becomes a collection of charts nobody checks, it adds noise instead of clarity.', 'Good dashboard planning starts with decisions, not widgets. The dashboard should show what needs action, what changed, what is blocked, and what the owner or team should review next.', ['Start with team decisions', 'Design tables before charts', 'Filter and search behavior', 'Roles and permissions', 'Alerts and exports', 'Dashboard review habits'], 'A service team may need a dashboard showing new requests, overdue follow-ups, pending quotes, unpaid invoices, and workload by employee. That is more useful than a beautiful chart that no one acts on.', 'If your team needs an admin dashboard that supports daily work, I can help plan and build it. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'laravel-dashboard-understand-business'),
    $post(3, 1, 'E-commerce Website Checklist Before You Spend Money on Ads', 'ecommerce-website-checklist-before-ads', 'E-commerce', ['E-commerce', 'Client Acquisition', 'Performance'], 'ecommerce website checklist before ads', 'store owners preparing paid campaigns', 'Ads can bring visitors to an e-commerce store, but they cannot fix unclear product pages, slow mobile checkout, hidden shipping costs, or weak trust signals.', 'Before spending on traffic, the store should be ready to answer buyer questions and complete orders without unnecessary doubt.', ['Product page readiness', 'Checkout and payment checks', 'Shipping and return clarity', 'Trust signals and reviews', 'Mobile speed', 'Tracking and campaign measurement'], 'A store selling skincare products should not run ads until product benefits, ingredients, shipping, returns, payment methods, reviews, and mobile checkout are clear and tested.', 'If you are preparing an e-commerce site for campaigns, I can help improve the store, checkout, and tracking before ad spend begins. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'plan-ecommerce-website-that-converts'),
    $post(3, 2, 'How to Turn Manual Business Processes Into Web App Features', 'turn-manual-business-processes-into-web-app-features', 'Business Automation', ['Business Automation', 'Custom Software', 'Dashboard'], 'automate manual business processes', 'business owners turning manual work into software', 'Manual processes are often the best blueprint for custom software. The trick is not to automate everything. The trick is to identify which steps are repeated, valuable, and ready to become features.', 'A web app feature should support a real workflow: intake, review, approval, payment, reporting, notification, or follow-up.', ['Map the current workflow', 'Find repeated decisions', 'Choose feature boundaries', 'Keep exceptions visible', 'Build admin tools', 'Measure time saved'], 'A company that manually approves supplier requests can turn the process into a web app with request forms, required documents, approval status, reviewer notes, notifications, and reports.', 'If you want to turn manual operations into a practical web app, I can help map and build the first version. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'automation-saves-small-business-hours'),
    $post(4, 0, 'The Difference Between a Cheap Website and a Professional Website', 'cheap-website-vs-professional-website', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'SEO', 'Performance'], 'cheap website vs professional website', 'business owners comparing website value and price', 'A cheap website and a professional website can both have pages, images, and a contact form. The difference is in planning, trust, speed, content, SEO structure, maintainability, and how well the website supports the business.', 'Price matters, but value depends on what the site must do after launch.', ['What cheap websites usually skip', 'What professional websites include', 'Speed and mobile quality', 'Copy, SEO, and trust', 'Ownership and maintenance', 'How to judge value'], 'A cheap site may look acceptable on a laptop but fail on mobile, miss search structure, load slowly, and provide no tracking. The hidden cost appears when leads do not come or updates become painful.', 'If you want a professional business website rather than a fragile online brochure, I can help plan and build it. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'real-cost-of-a-cheap-website'),
    $post(4, 1, 'How to Scope a Laravel Project Without Losing Control of the Budget', 'scope-laravel-project-without-losing-budget', 'Laravel', ['Laravel', 'Custom Software', 'Deployment'], 'Laravel project scope budget', 'founders and owners planning Laravel applications', 'Laravel projects can grow quickly when every idea becomes a feature. Good scoping protects budget by defining the first useful version and leaving the roadmap for later.', 'Scope control is not about lowering quality. It is about building the right foundation without pretending every future feature is needed immediately.', ['Define the core workflow', 'Separate modules from features', 'Estimate admin work', 'Plan integrations carefully', 'Budget for deployment and maintenance', 'Use milestones and review points'], 'A CRM project may start with leads, clients, tasks, notes, and reporting. Advanced automations, complex permissions, and document generation can be planned as later modules unless they are essential to launch.', 'If you need help scoping a Laravel application before development starts, I can help you define a realistic first version. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'laravel-business-applications-strong-choice'),
    $post(4, 2, 'What Makes a SaaS Landing Page Ready for Real Users', 'saas-landing-page-ready-for-real-users', 'SaaS & MVP', ['SaaS', 'MVP', 'Client Acquisition'], 'SaaS landing page checklist', 'SaaS founders preparing to validate or launch', 'A SaaS landing page is ready when a real visitor can understand the problem, see the promise, trust the product direction, and take the next step without confusion.', 'The page does not need to describe every feature. It needs to explain the core workflow and why the first version is worth trying.', ['Clear positioning', 'Problem and promise', 'Feature explanation without overload', 'Proof without fake claims', 'Signup or demo flow', 'Analytics and feedback capture'], 'A SaaS for invoice reminders should explain who it helps, what repeated task it removes, how reminders work, what users see, and how a founder can request early access or book a demo.', 'If you are preparing a SaaS landing page and MVP, I can help shape the message and build the first product path. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'build-saas-mvp-without-wasting-budget'),
    $post(5, 0, 'How AI Can Improve Lead Capture on a Business Website', 'ai-improve-lead-capture-business-website', 'AI & Productivity', ['AI Tools', 'Business Automation', 'Client Acquisition'], 'AI lead capture website', 'business owners considering AI-assisted lead workflows', 'AI can improve lead capture when it helps classify, summarize, route, or respond to inquiries. It should support the sales process, not make promises on behalf of the business.', 'The best first AI feature is often internal: helping the team understand and respond to leads faster.', ['AI-assisted form summaries', 'Lead qualification and routing', 'Draft replies with human review', 'Chat support boundaries', 'CRM integration', 'Risks and privacy considerations'], 'A web agency can use AI to summarize project inquiries by budget, timeline, service type, and urgency, then route qualified leads to the right person for review.', 'If you want AI lead capture added carefully to your website or CRM, I can help design the workflow and build it. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'ai-tools-improve-small-business-website'),
    $post(5, 1, 'Website Maintenance: What Business Owners Usually Ignore', 'website-maintenance-business-owners-ignore', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'Security', 'Performance'], 'website maintenance for business', 'business owners responsible for keeping websites healthy', 'A website is not finished forever on launch day. Content changes, software updates, forms break, pages slow down, security risks appear, and business offers evolve.', 'Maintenance protects the value of the original build. It also prevents small issues from becoming expensive emergencies.', ['Security updates and backups', 'Content and service changes', 'Form and email testing', 'Speed and image review', 'SEO checks and redirects', 'Analytics review'], 'A business may not notice that a contact form stopped sending emails until inquiries drop. A monthly maintenance routine can catch that kind of issue before it affects revenue.', 'If your business website needs a practical maintenance plan, I can help review, improve, and support it. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'real-cost-of-a-cheap-website'),
    $post(5, 2, 'How to Choose Between WordPress, Laravel, and No-Code Tools', 'choose-wordpress-laravel-no-code-tools', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'Laravel', 'Custom Software'], 'WordPress vs Laravel vs no-code', 'non-technical clients choosing a platform', 'WordPress, Laravel, and no-code tools can all be useful. The right choice depends on content editing, custom workflows, budget, ownership, maintenance, and future plans.', 'The decision should start with what the business needs the system to do, not with which tool sounds popular.', ['When WordPress fits', 'When Laravel fits', 'When no-code fits', 'Ownership and maintenance tradeoffs', 'Custom logic and integrations', 'Decision checklist'], 'A consultant with a simple content site may choose WordPress. A founder building a subscription dashboard may choose Laravel. A team validating a workflow may test no-code before investing in custom development.', 'If you need help choosing the right technical direction before spending money, contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'choose-tech-stack-business-web-app'),
    $post(6, 0, 'How to Build Trust With a New Visitor in the First 10 Seconds', 'build-trust-new-visitor-first-10-seconds', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'Client Acquisition', 'SEO'], 'build trust on website', 'business owners improving website trust and first impressions', 'A new visitor decides quickly whether a website feels relevant, credible, and safe enough to continue. The first screen must answer what you do, who you help, and why the visitor should trust you.', 'Trust is built through clarity, proof, design quality, speed, and a contact path that does not feel risky.', ['Homepage message clarity', 'Visible proof near claims', 'Professional visual hierarchy', 'Fast mobile loading', 'Contact confidence', 'Mistakes that create doubt'], 'A consulting business can build trust faster by showing who it helps, what problems it solves, selected proof, a clear process, and a contact option that explains what happens next.', 'If your website needs to build trust faster with new visitors, I can help improve the strategy, copy, and build. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'build-trust-website-before-contact'),
    $post(6, 1, 'Custom Software vs SaaS Tools: Which One Should a Business Choose?', 'custom-software-vs-saas-tools-business', 'SaaS & MVP', ['SaaS', 'Custom Software', 'Business Automation'], 'custom software vs SaaS tools', 'business owners deciding whether to buy or build', 'Buying a SaaS tool is often the fastest path. Building custom software makes sense when the workflow is specific, repeated, valuable, and hard to fit into generic tools.', 'The decision is not about pride of ownership. It is about cost, flexibility, speed, maintenance, and business fit.', ['When SaaS tools are enough', 'When custom software makes sense', 'Integration and data ownership', 'Cost over time', 'Maintenance responsibility', 'Hybrid approaches'], 'A small team may start with a generic CRM. Later, if quoting, documents, customer portals, and reporting need a custom workflow, building a focused Laravel system may become sensible.', 'If you are unsure whether to buy software or build a custom system, I can help you compare the options. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'turn-service-business-into-simple-saas'),
    $post(6, 2, 'How a Client Portal Can Improve Your Service Business', 'client-portal-improve-service-business', 'Business Automation', ['Business Automation', 'Custom Software', 'Dashboard'], 'client portal for service business', 'service business owners who manage ongoing client work', 'A client portal gives customers one place to see updates, documents, invoices, requests, and project status. It can reduce back-and-forth and make a service business feel more organized.', 'A portal is useful when clients regularly ask for information that could be safely shown through a private account.', ['What a client portal includes', 'Documents and invoices', 'Project or request status', 'Secure login and permissions', 'Notifications', 'Admin workflow behind the portal'], 'An agency can use a portal to show project milestones, upload documents, collect approvals, and keep invoices in one place instead of spreading updates across email threads.', 'If your service business needs a client portal or dashboard, I can help plan and build it in Laravel. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'difference-between-website-and-web-application'),
    $post(7, 0, 'How to Prepare Your Business Website for International Clients', 'prepare-business-website-international-clients', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'Client Acquisition', 'SEO'], 'website for international clients', 'business owners, freelancers, and agencies serving global clients', 'A website for international clients needs more than a translated headline. It needs clear positioning, trust signals, time-zone awareness, payment or contact clarity, and language that makes remote collaboration feel safe.', 'Global visitors may not know your local reputation. The website must explain who you help, what you build, how you work, and how a first conversation starts.', ['Global positioning', 'Remote work trust signals', 'Clear services and process', 'Contact and time-zone clarity', 'Currency and payment expectations', 'International SEO basics'], 'A freelance developer targeting global clients should show services, selected work, process, technology strengths, English communication, remote availability, and a clear contact path.', 'If you want your website to attract international clients for web development or digital services, I can help plan and build it. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'portfolio-website-convert-visitors-clients'),
    $post(7, 1, 'The Practical Guide to Payment Integration for Web Apps', 'practical-guide-payment-integration-web-apps', 'SaaS & MVP', ['SaaS', 'API', 'E-commerce'], 'payment integration web app', 'founders and business owners adding payments to web apps', 'Payment integration is not only adding a checkout button. It affects pricing, invoices, taxes, subscription status, failed payments, refunds, permissions, customer emails, and support workflows.', 'A payment flow should be planned like a business process, not a technical checkbox.', ['Payment methods and providers', 'One-time payments vs subscriptions', 'Checkout and customer records', 'Webhooks and payment status', 'Invoices and refunds', 'Security and testing'], 'A SaaS MVP may start with manual billing, then add Stripe or PayPal once the paid workflow is proven. That can reduce early complexity while keeping the architecture ready.', 'If you need payment integration for a SaaS, portal, or e-commerce project, I can help plan and implement it carefully. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'plan-ecommerce-website-that-converts'),
    $post(7, 2, 'How to Use Analytics to Improve a Business Website', 'use-analytics-improve-business-website', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'SEO', 'Client Acquisition'], 'website analytics for business', 'business owners who want useful website data', 'Analytics should help a business make better decisions. The goal is not to stare at charts. The goal is to understand which pages attract visitors, which actions matter, and where the website loses trust or clarity.', 'Good analytics starts with questions, not tools. What do you need to know to improve the website?', ['Traffic sources', 'Important pages', 'Form and click tracking', 'Lead quality review', 'Content performance', 'Monthly improvement routine'], 'A service website may discover that blog posts bring traffic but service pages convert better. Internal links and clearer CTAs can connect those readers to the right next step.', 'If you want analytics set up in a way that improves decisions rather than creating noise, I can help. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'business-website-before-running-ads'),
    $post(8, 0, 'How to Plan User Roles and Permissions in a Business Web App', 'plan-user-roles-permissions-business-web-app', 'Laravel', ['Laravel', 'Security', 'Custom Software'], 'user roles permissions web app', 'founders and owners planning private web applications', 'Roles and permissions decide who can see, create, edit, approve, export, or delete information. If they are planned late, the application can become risky or difficult to change.', 'Permissions are a business design problem before they are a code problem.', ['Identify user types', 'Map actions to roles', 'Protect sensitive data', 'Admin and audit needs', 'Permission mistakes', 'Laravel implementation considerations'], 'A client portal might include owners, staff, clients, and accountants. Each role needs different access to documents, invoices, messages, and reports.', 'If your business web app needs clear roles and permissions, I can help design and build that foundation. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'laravel-business-applications-strong-choice'),
    $post(8, 1, 'Why Your Website Speed Affects Leads, Trust, and Sales', 'website-speed-affects-leads-trust-sales', 'Web Development', ['Performance', 'Web Development', 'Client Acquisition'], 'website speed affects conversions', 'business owners who want faster websites and better leads', 'Website speed affects how visitors feel before they read your offer. A slow page creates doubt, especially on mobile, and makes every marketing channel less efficient.', 'Performance is not only a technical score. It is part of trust, usability, search visibility, and conversion.', ['Mobile speed and first impression', 'Image and script weight', 'Hosting and caching', 'Core pages to test', 'Speed and ad performance', 'Maintenance habits'], 'A landing page with heavy images and scripts may look polished on a fast office connection but feel broken on mobile data. Compressing images and removing unused scripts can improve trust quickly.', 'If your website feels slow or wastes paid traffic, I can help audit and improve performance. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'real-cost-of-a-cheap-website'),
    $post(8, 2, 'How to Create a Content Strategy That Supports Your Services', 'content-strategy-supports-your-services', 'Freelance & Digital Business', ['SEO', 'Client Acquisition', 'Web Development'], 'content strategy for service business', 'freelancers, consultants, agencies, and service businesses', 'A service business blog should not publish random articles. Content should answer buyer questions, support service pages, build trust, and guide readers toward a useful next step.', 'Good content strategy connects search intent to business intent. It helps readers make decisions while showing how you think.', ['Service page support', 'Buyer questions', 'Content clusters', 'Internal links', 'Proof and examples', 'Review and update rhythm'], 'A Laravel developer can publish articles about dashboards, CRM planning, SaaS MVP scope, and web app security. Each piece helps clients understand the work before they contact.', 'If you want a blog strategy that supports client acquisition instead of random publishing, I can help plan the system. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'portfolio-website-convert-visitors-clients'),
    $post(9, 0, 'How to Validate a SaaS Idea Before Paying for Development', 'validate-saas-idea-before-development', 'SaaS & MVP', ['SaaS', 'MVP', 'Startup'], 'validate SaaS idea before development', 'startup founders before investing in development', 'A SaaS idea should be tested before a large build. Validation does not need to be complicated. It needs honest conversations, a clear promise, a simple landing page, and a way to measure real interest.', 'The purpose of validation is to reduce guesswork before development costs grow.', ['Define the painful workflow', 'Talk to real prospects', 'Test a landing page', 'Use manual delivery first', 'Measure willingness to pay', 'Decide what to build next'], 'A founder can validate a reporting SaaS by manually preparing reports for a few target customers, then turning the repeated parts into software after demand is clearer.', 'If you want to validate and scope a SaaS idea before development, I can help you plan the first serious test. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'founder-mistakes-first-mvp'),
    $post(9, 1, 'What Business Owners Should Know About Web App Security', 'web-app-security-for-business-owners', 'Web Development', ['Security', 'Web Development', 'Laravel'], 'web app security for business owners', 'non-technical business owners responsible for web apps', 'Web app security is not only a developer concern. Business owners should understand the basics because security affects customer trust, data privacy, operations, and long-term maintenance.', 'You do not need to know every attack type. You do need to know what responsible development should include.', ['Authentication and passwords', 'Roles and permissions', 'Input validation', 'Backups and recovery', 'Updates and dependencies', 'Logging and monitoring'], 'A small portal that stores invoices and customer documents needs stronger protection than a public brochure website. That affects login, permissions, storage, backups, and support processes.', 'If your business web app needs a security-minded Laravel foundation, I can help plan and build it properly. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'laravel-business-applications-strong-choice'),
    $post(9, 2, 'How to Create Better Contact Forms That Actually Bring Leads', 'better-contact-forms-that-bring-leads', 'Web Development', ['Client Acquisition', 'Web Development', 'CRM'], 'contact form conversion tips', 'business owners improving lead capture', 'A contact form should make it easy for the right person to start a conversation. Many forms fail because they are too vague, too long, too hidden, or disconnected from follow-up.', 'A better form qualifies leads gently without creating friction.', ['Ask the right fields', 'Reduce form anxiety', 'Connect forms to CRM or email', 'Confirmation and response expectations', 'Spam protection', 'Tracking form quality'], 'A web development inquiry form might ask about project type, budget range, timeline, current website, and business goal. That helps both sides have a better first conversation.', 'If your website needs better forms and lead follow-up, I can help design and build the flow. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'business-website-before-running-ads'),
    $post(10, 0, 'How to Plan a Multi-Language Website for Global Visitors', 'plan-multi-language-website-global-visitors', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'SEO', 'Client Acquisition'], 'multilingual website planning', 'business owners serving international visitors', 'A multi-language website is not only translation. It affects URL structure, SEO, content maintenance, calls to action, support expectations, and how global visitors understand the offer.', 'Planning languages early prevents messy content and search problems later.', ['Choose languages by business value', 'URL and SEO structure', 'Translation quality and review', 'Localized calls to action', 'Maintenance workflow', 'Common multilingual mistakes'], 'A SaaS company targeting English and French markets should plan language-specific pages, metadata, support expectations, and content updates before duplicating the site.', 'If you need a multi-language website planned for global visitors, I can help with structure, development, and launch checks. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'portfolio-website-convert-visitors-clients'),
    $post(10, 1, 'How to Turn a Blog Into a Client Acquisition System', 'turn-blog-into-client-acquisition-system', 'Freelance & Digital Business', ['SEO', 'Client Acquisition', 'Web Development'], 'blog for client acquisition', 'freelancers, agencies, consultants, and business owners', 'A blog becomes a client acquisition system when it answers real buyer questions, supports service pages, shows judgment, and guides readers toward a relevant next step.', 'The goal is not to publish more. The goal is to publish useful articles that make your expertise easier to trust.', ['Choose topics from buyer questions', 'Connect posts to services', 'Use internal links intentionally', 'Add soft CTAs', 'Update old posts', 'Measure inquiries and quality'], 'A consultant can publish articles about project planning, pricing, maintenance, and mistakes. Those posts help readers prepare and make the contact conversation more serious.', 'If you want a blog that supports real client acquisition, I can help plan the content system and technical structure. Contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'portfolio-website-convert-visitors-clients'),
    $post(10, 2, 'The Complete Web Project Launch Checklist for Business Owners', 'web-project-launch-checklist-business-owners', 'Web Development', ['Web Development', 'Deployment', 'SEO'], 'website launch checklist business', 'business owners and founders preparing to launch', 'A web project launch is more than pushing code live. It includes content, forms, SEO metadata, analytics, redirects, images, performance, security, backups, and a post-launch review plan.', 'A checklist protects the project from small oversights that are easy to miss when everyone is focused on the launch date.', ['Content and page review', 'SEO metadata and redirects', 'Forms and email delivery', 'Analytics and events', 'Speed and mobile testing', 'Backups, security, and launch monitoring'], 'A business website may look ready, but the launch checklist catches missing meta descriptions, oversized images, an untested contact form, old URLs without redirects, and analytics that never recorded conversions.', 'If you want help launching a website, Laravel app, dashboard, or SaaS MVP with fewer avoidable mistakes, contact me at https://youssefyouyou.com/contact.', 'what-to-prepare-before-hiring-web-developer'),
